				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "is91uixwTy+stsz3qxgw9Q=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "This page describes a small model for investigating memory in a running image, by people or by agents. It complements [[Analysing the size of the image]], which explains what a saved image contains.\n\nTwo questions are useful when memory grows: **what kinds of objects** take the space, and **who holds them**. A space tally answers the first question quickly. The memory-space model answers the second one: it walks the objects reachable from chosen roots and attributes their memory to the root that reaches them first. Neither answer is exact, and they do not have to be: the goal is to see quickly where space is spent."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-17T23:17:30.075865+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-17T23:17:30.075865+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "XzFCFYMRRs+ECBGUIGPhRg=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "A few objects, each with one job:\n- a {{gtClass:GtMemorySpaceRootsDefinition}} says where to look: ordered groups of roots, where to stop, and which kinds of objects to tag. It is configured in a snippet, without writing a class;\n- a {{gtClass:GtMemorySpaceRootGroup}} is a named group of roots ({{gtClass:GtMemorySpaceRoot}}), computed when the estimation runs. Its class side has ready-made groups for the class-side state of all classes (by package) and for the globals;\n- a {{gtClass:GtMemorySpaceBoundary}} says at which classes a walk stops (by default code entities and processes) and which classes are tagged;\n- a {{gtClass:GtMemorySpaceEstimator}} walks the objects, counting each object once, by identity;\n- a {{gtClass:GtMemorySpaceEstimate}} holds the result: memory per category (where it comes from), per tag (what kind of objects), per root and per group of roots.\n\nGroups are estimated in order. An object reachable from several groups is counted in the first one, so put specific roots first and roots that reach almost everything last."
						},
