				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## Recipe 1: what kinds of objects take space"
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-17T23:17:30.08144+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-17T23:17:30.08144+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "BcxbtmQcQhutCYbcrKpgjw=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "Describe the roots in the order in which they should claim memory, then inspect the estimation. The Root groups and Roots views show who holds what; Categories split the class-side state by package. Walking a large heap takes minutes (about 150 thousand objects per second in a heap of 4 GB), so start with a few groups."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "pharoSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-17T23:17:30.08171+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-17T23:17:30.08171+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "IrfFfVgpSDO0gFm0UDhzvQ=="
							},
							"code" : "\"Who holds memory: the Lepiter databases first, then the class-side state of all classes and the globals.\nThe walk stops at code entities, processes and Bloc spaces.\"\n| definition |\ndefinition := GtMemorySpaceRootsDefinition new\n\troots: 'Lepiter databases'\n\t\tare: [ LeDatabasesRegistry default currentLoadedDefaultLogicalDatabase\n\t\t\t\tifNil: [ #() ]\n\t\t\t\tifNotNil: [ :aLogicalDatabase | aLogicalDatabase databases ] ];\n\trootGroup: GtMemorySpaceRootGroup classSideState;\n\trootGroup: GtMemorySpaceRootGroup globals;\n\tstopAtInstancesOf: { BlSpace };\n\ttag: #string instancesOf: { ByteString. WideString };\n\texpectedObjects: 5000000;\n\tyourself.\ndefinition estimate"
						}
					]
				},
